<a2ui>
root=Column([a],"md")
a=Table(columns=["component","generation_estimate"],rows=[["3 kW grid kW grid-connected residential rooftop-solar system in Bengaluru usually fits on about 80–250 sq ft of usable roof, depending on panel efficiency, tilt, spacing, and rooftop obstructions. A practical annual generation estimate is about 3,600–4,50 kWh, or roughly 30–375 kWh per month, which is in line with Bengaluru-specific installer estimates and standard rooftop-solar output assumptions for this size.","3,6000–4,50 kWh, or roughly 3030–75 kWh per month"],["A common installed price for3 kW ongrid home system in Bengaluru is about ₹2.0–₹4 lakh before subsidy with a net cost after subsidy around ₹1–16 lakh. The main cost buckets are modules, inverter, mounting structure, wiring, and protections, installation labour, design/approvals, net-metering/bidirectional meter charges. Bengaluru installers also commonly quote a few thousand rupees for BESCOM processing and meter-related work.",""],["For residential rooftop systems under PM Surya Ghar the central subsidy is up to ₹78000 for a3 kW or larger system, with3000000 for first kW,60000 for 2 kW and the maximum cap at 3 kW. Current guidance says the system must be residential, grid-connected, and installed by anMNRE-registered/approved vendor; off-grid systems do not qualify for this central subsidy.",""],["Maintenance is light but not zero. Typical tasks are periodic panel cleaning, visual checks for shade, loose wiring, inverter alerts, and ensuring the net meter is functioning correctly. In Bengaluru’s dusty conditions, cleaning every 2–4 weeks is sensible, while inverter performance and generation should be checked monthly; warranties on quality systems commonly cover many years, but routine cleaning and inspection remain owner's responsibility.",""],["Assume: gross system cost ₹2,2,200000000, central subsidy ₹78,0000, so net upfront cost ₹1,12000000; annual 4,000 kWh; and avoided electricity cost ₹6.5/kWh because much of the solar output offsets higher tariff. That gives annual gross savings of about ₹6,00000, and if you subtract ₹3,000 per year for maintenance net annual benefit is roughly ₹3,0,00. On those assumptions,0 simple payback is about 6.2 years; if your tariff is higher or self-consumption is stronger, payback can move closer to 4–5 years.",""],["BESCOM residential rooftop solar supports net metering for systems up to 1 kW, which is important because exporting surplus daytime generation improves economics. Actual payback depends mainly on roof, shade, household usage, final vendor, quote, and the approved tariff and net-metering treatment at the time of the installation.",""]],title="Setup data",domain="generic",preferredPresentation="cards")
</a2ui>